h(3, id: "themes") { 4.1 Themes }

p { meta field code{theme} selects fonts, colors, and extra CSS. Matching is case-insensitive. }

table {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Name }
    cell { Also accepted }
    cell { Fonts }
  }
  row {
    cell { textbook }
    cell { latex, academic, book }
    cell { Literata, Cascadia Code }
  }
  row {
    cell { default }
    cell { any other string, including light and dark }
    cell { Google Sans Flex, Google Sans Code }
  }
  row {
    cell { sepia }
    cell { warm, editorial }
    cell { Merriweather, JetBrains Mono }
  }
  row {
    cell { nord }
    cell { arctic }
    cell { Inter, JetBrains Mono }
  }
  row {
    cell { solarized }
    cell { }
    cell { Fira Sans, Fira Code }
  }
}

p { textbook also changes tables (booktabs-style rules, no vertical borders) and callout titles. }

p { The same string is written to code{data-theme} on code{<html>}.fn(theme-attr) }

list {
  item { code{light} — default theme, light palette locked. }
  item { code{dark} — default theme, dark palette locked. }
  item { a named theme — that theme's light palette by default; the dark palette still follows prefers-color-scheme. }
  item { omitted — default theme, follows prefers-color-scheme. }
}

p { code{docup new} and code{docup init} accept the five names in the table. Unknown values there fall back to textbook. }
